* The language computer: open and shut with a click, picked up any time
* (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own scripts in place of the game's).
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
* any world: it changes objects by kind, not Eden's map, so it runs on every
* world (other Additions run only on worlds started from Eden.sfc).
*
* The computer (2 9 28, "lapt", by the submarine's east door) speaks through
* a blackboard (3 3 11) kept out of sight at 4300, 640, and has a light arrow
* (2 1 55) that points at it while it is shut. The game's activate script
* opened it, talked for 20 seconds and shut it again in one go, and made it
* not carryable while it did; a click during that did nothing (ACTV 1 has no
* click action), so an open computer could neither be shut nor picked up
* (owner, 2026-11-23: "a right click anywhere on its sprites should be able
* to pick it up, whether open or closed, and a left click anywhere on its
* sprites should open or close it").
*
* Now a click opens a shut computer, which then talks (teaching a word, as
* before) and stays open, and a click on an open one shuts it, ending the
* talk. A creature pushing an open one has it talk again. It can be picked
* up at any time, open or shut; a pickup ends the talk and leaves it as it
* was. OV00: 1 while open.

* activate 1: the hand's click or a creature's push
scrp 2 9 28 1
  setv actv 0
  doif movs eq 0 and grav eq 0
    doif ov00 eq 0
      setv ov00 1
      gsub open
      gsub talk
    else
      doif from ne pntr
        gsub talk
      else
        setv ov00 0
        gsub hush
        gsub clos
      endi
    endi
  endi
  stop
  subr open
    enum 2 1 55 mesg writ targ 5 mvto 4300 640 next
    base 0
    anim [1234567]
    over
  retn
  subr talk
    base 7
    anim [01234567R]
    setv var0 posx
    subv var0 10
    setv var1 posy
    wait 10
    enum 3 3 11 mesg wrt+ targ 256 var0 var1 0 next
    wait 200
    base 0
    pose 7
  retn
  subr hush
    enum 3 3 11 mesg writ targ 257 next
  retn
  subr clos
    base 0
    anim [6543210]
    over
    mesg wrt+ ownr 256 0 0 0
  retn
endm

* pickup: the talk ends; an open computer stays open
scrp 2 9 28 4
  enum 2 1 55 mvto 4300 640 next
  enum 3 3 11 mesg writ targ 257 next
  base 0
  doif ov00 eq 1
    pose 7
  else
    pose 0
  endi
endm

* drop: the arrow comes back beside it once it lands, if it is shut
scrp 2 9 28 5
  loop
    wait 1
  untl grav eq 0
  doif ov00 eq 0
    mesg wrt+ ownr 256 0 0 0
  endi
endm

* the blackboard's talk cut short: back out of sight (a message ends the
* talk script running on it)
scrp 3 3 11 257
  mvto 4300 640
endm

* every computer carryable and answering clicks, shown open or shut as it
* was left (a talk cut short by a save goes quiet)
enum 2 9 28
  setv attr 199
  setv actv 0
  base 0
  doif ov00 eq 1
    pose 7
  else
    pose 0
    mesg wrt+ targ 256 0 0 0
  endi
next
